{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3082","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3082","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3082\",\"parent_revision\":\"e09a352450bf0c5a9f8a7da41864c3a88b36a5d7\",\"root_revision\":\"3eb587abce74e7694fe28d0b048c5d963c98d809ed2d5920abf84a795e529b03\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nNamed as a known gap in ADR-3075-4, not solved there. Control-set entries can hold full\\ngenerated documents \u2014 ADR-3072-1's known limitation already establishes this is not\\nhypothetical: item #2953 alone generates an estimated 270,946+ tokens. Without a cleanup\\nmechanism for `\\\\$DH_STATE_HOME/sessions/{id}/` directories after a session ends, entries\\naccumulate on disk unboundedly across every session ever run.\\n\\n`get-gate-token.mjs` (the precedent ADR-3075-4 follows) never faced this \u2014 a single small token\\nfile has no meaningful accumulation cost. A control-set store holding full generated documents\\ndoes.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBlocked on #3062 (control set must exist first) and ADR-3075-4 (out-of-process, session-keyed\\nstore \u2014 the design this accumulation hazard is specific to).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Session-keyed control-set directories are removed (or become eligible for removal) after\\n      their session ends, not retained indefinitely\\n- [ ] The cleanup mechanism does not depend on the session process cleanly exiting (crashes,\\n      kills, and abrupt termination must not leave the directory permanently orphaned)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"23a3ed40f2cd81afa079c6090e2059eea6fa47083d2f80b62ede9a2f7e7a7b82\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABP85CsQ\"}"}